14Z"},"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-03-06T17:21:04Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T15:22:22Z","closed_at":"2025-07-15T15:22:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4\n- Does not occur in 4.3\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 1920x1080 display\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen querying collision using `PhysicsDirectSpaceState2D.intersect_point(...)`, when in full screen resolution in project setting, the detection is wrong and appears shifted.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a staticBody2D with a collision shape.\nSet the viewport width and height in project setting to screen resolution (1920x1080)\n\nTry to detect a mouse event with something like :\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _unhandled_input(event):\n\tif event.is_action_pressed(\"ui_select\"):\n\t\tvar pos = get_global_mouse_position()\n\t\tvar params := PhysicsPointQueryParameters2D.new()\n\t\tparams.position = pos\n\t\tparams.collide_with_areas = true\n\t\tparams.collide_with_bodies = true\n\t\tvar results = get_world_2d().direct_space_state.intersect_point(params)\n\t\tprint(results)\n\n```\n\nThe shape is detected about 100px below its actual position.\n\nIf the screen resolution is not full screen, everything works as expected.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19112779/project.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_us